### Update: Icon-Only Light/Dark Mode Toggle with Local Bootstrap Icons

We will modify your existing ASP.NET Core MVC .NET 8 application without recreating the project or changing its existing MVC structure.

The updated implementation will use locally installed Bootstrap Icons, JavaScript, CSS, and browser Local Storage.

### 1\. Expected final appearance

### My Application

Light Mode

Switch to Dark Mode

### My Application

Dark Mode

Switch to Light Mode

Illustrative navbar appearance. The actual button will contain only the Bootstrap moon or sun icon, without visible text.

### Expected behavior

| Current theme | Visible icon    | Accessible label     | Saved value |
| ------------- | --------------- | -------------------- | ----------- |
| Light Mode    | bi bi-moon-fill | Switch to Dark Mode  | light       |
| Dark Mode     | bi bi-sun-fill  | Switch to Light Mode | dark        |

The implementation will also:

* Remove visible button text.

* Keep the button compact and centered.

* Use `blur()` only for mouse and touch interactions, not keyboard interactions.

* Preserve a visible keyboard focus indicator.

* Load the saved theme before the page's stylesheets to minimize theme flashing.

* Avoid duplicate click event listeners.

* Work offline after Bootstrap Icons has been installed locally.

### 2\. Files we will modify

| File                        | Modification                                                            |
| --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml | Local Bootstrap Icons CSS, early theme initialization, icon-only button |
| wwwroot/js/theme.js         | Theme loading, switching, storage, icons, accessibility, focus handling |
| wwwroot/css/theme.css       | Compact button, hover, focus, and theme styles                          |
| libman.json                 | Add Bootstrap Icons library                                             |

We will not modify `Program.cs`, controllers, models, database configuration, or existing MVC pages.

### 3\. Install Bootstrap Icons locally using LibMan

