### Important placement instructions

| Code                       | Exact location                             |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Early theme initialization | Inside <head>, immediately after meta tags |
| Bootstrap Icons CSS        | Inside <head>, before </head>              |
| Theme CSS                  | After site.css                             |
| Icon-only button           | Inside the existing navbar                 |
| Bootstrap JS               | Before </body>                             |
| theme.js                   | After Bootstrap JS, before </body>         |

Why does the early script and `theme.js` both read the theme?

They have different responsibilities:

* The early script applies the saved preference before the browser renders the page.

* `theme.js` initializes the button, attaches the click event, and updates its accessibility attributes.

This separation prevents unnecessary visual flashing while keeping the JavaScript organized.

