### 9\. Testing instructions

We should test not only whether the icon changes, but also whether the application behaves correctly across different input methods.

### Test 1 — Initial page load

* Open your application.

* Open Developer Tools.

* Go to Application → Local Storage.

* Remove the existing `theme` key.

* Refresh the page.

Expected result:

* If the operating system prefers Light Mode, the moon icon appears.

* If the operating system prefers Dark Mode, the sun icon appears.

* No visible button text appears.

* The theme is applied before the main page styles render.

### Test 2 — Mouse interaction

* Click the moon icon.

* Verify that Dark Mode is applied.

* Verify that the moon changes into the sun.

* Move your mouse away from the button.

Expected result:

* Dark Mode is active.

* The button label is `Switch to Light Mode`.

* The title is `Switch to Light Mode`.

* The button does not remain visually focused after the click.

Repeat the test using the sun icon.

### Test 3 — Touch interaction

If using a touchscreen laptop or mobile browser:

* Open the application.

* Tap the moon icon.

* Verify that the theme changes.

* Check that the button does not remain visually focused.

The `event.detail > 0` check handles normal pointer-generated mouse and touch clicks. Some assistive technologies generate clicks differently, so those should also be tested separately.

### Test 4 — Keyboard interaction

This is an important accessibility test.

* Refresh the application.

* Press `Tab` until the theme button receives focus.

* Check whether a visible focus outline appears.

* Press `Enter`.

* Check whether the theme changes.

* Verify that keyboard focus remains on the theme button.

* Press `Space` to toggle again.

Keyboard focus should remain on the button after both Enter and Space activation.

### Test 5 — Local Storage

Open the browser Console.

Execute:

```javascript
localStorage.getItem("theme");
```

Expected results:

| Selected theme | Console result |
| -------------- | -------------- |
